    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for the Austin Waves leans heavily into situational advantages, headlined by **Kyle Tucker** (65.86) and **Gunnar Henderson** (63.39). While **Kyle Tucker** faces a formidable arm in Ray, his elite base production and prime order slot in the 5-hole anchor our outfield. **Gunnar Henderson** remains a must-start despite facing a tough southpaw like Fried; the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and wind blowing out provides enough of an offensive ceiling to overcome the negative platoon split. Meanwhile, **Sam Antonacci** (60.17) emerges as a high-upside play at the top of the order against Lugo; his impressive 0.391 xwOBA and the leadoff designation make him a crucial engine for run production today.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) on the bench. Despite his pedigree and a solid park factor, he is sidelined by a combination of a lower daily efficiency score relative to our infield starters and a challenging matchup against an elite arm in Jax. We are also monitoring the risks associated with **Heliot Ramos** (43.69), whose score was significantly suppressed due to a negative SP skill adjustment against Ohtani. Although **Heliot Ramos** is active, he is our lowest-ranked starter and represents the greatest volatility risk in the lineup today. We continue to hold **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, but remain confident that the depth provided by **Liam Hicks** (59.93) and **Andy Pages** (60.00) provides the necessary stability to navigate this slate without forcing suboptimal matchups.",
